## V-28 — what I checked that the report did not

The report was thorough and honestly self-critical, so the value was in the angles it *didn't* run:

- **Namespace parity with the producer.** A consumer-side comparison is worthless if it compares a
  different namespace than the producer writes. Re-derived both sides: `migrate.ts` resolves the
  same two directories, applies the same `.sql` filter, and inserts a bare basename (`file.name`)
  on *both* write paths — including the reconciled-not-executed renumber path. The new script
  compares bare basenames. No skew, in either direction.
- **My own mutation, aimed at the gap the builder admitted its structural test cannot see.** The
  report states a `> 0` → `> 1` mutant would leave the structural test green. I ran it: **2 of 16
  tests fail.** The boundary is covered behaviourally. Restored; sha256 back to baseline.
- **Corroboration of the builder's restore.** My independent baseline hash begins `f1fc63a5…` —
  identical to the sha256 the report cites. Their mutation-proof restore was genuine, not asserted.
- Tests re-run, not taken on report: **16/16**, and **177/177** for the full directory.

**One real hazard found (R-28.1, routed to ADHIKĀRIN, low now):** the
`if (process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'test')` entrypoint guard makes this **gate** a silent `exit 0` with
zero output under `NODE_ENV=test` — I ran it and confirmed. Not reachable at either committed
invocation site. But `ci.yml` already sets job-level `NODE_ENV: test` on three jobs, and `ci.yml`
is the natural future home for a check like this. `dispatch_gate.ts:175` carries the identical guard.

## V-29 — the decisive question was whether criterion 9's FAIL(23) → PASS(0) was earned

It was. D-42 forbids detector shift, so I treated this as the campaign's central risk and probed
the detector three ways in memory (the real artifact was never written to):

| probe | result |
|---|---|
| inject a synthetic 24th packet | `n_unresolved` 0 → **1**, new `UNMAPPED` bucket appears |
| declassify one SHADOWED packet | 0 → **1** (`ka_tulana`) |
| remove the SHADOWED disposition | 0 → **5** (all five named) |

The zero is a computed result with three live paths to non-zero. I also confirmed D-38 part 3
holds what the generator quotes — **verbatim**, and it names this exit criterion explicitly — and
re-derived all 23 reading classes from `ZERO_CONSUMER_EVIDENCE_v1_0.md` §2 by parsing the source
table: **zero drift**, no SHADOWED silently softened to INPUT-ONLY.

Also: `reading_history` append-only verified by diff against `9001576e8` (first 4 entries
byte-identical); the register generator reproduces its artifacts byte-identically apart from
timestamps, so nothing was hand-edited; and the declared side effect on
`asset_catalogue_disclosed_residuals.json` touches only the **non-gating** block, exactly as claimed.

